# token-lab — reference CLAUDE.md (the "after" for Section 4)

> The repo intentionally ships WITHOUT a root CLAUDE.md. In Section 4 participants
> create one. This file is the reference answer — the facilitator stages it on
> the `after/config` branch. Copy it to the repo root as `CLAUDE.md`.

## What this is
Full-stack TS sandbox for a token-spend workshop. FE (Vite/React) + API (Express) + Postgres, all in Docker.

## How to run things — ALWAYS via Docker, never locally
- Start everything: `docker compose up -d`
- API logs: `docker compose logs -f api`
- Reseed DB: `docker compose exec api npm run seed`
- Query DB: `docker compose exec db psql -U tokenlab -d tokenlab`
- Run the eval: `npm run eval -- --label <name> --task <id>`

## Layout
- `api/src/index.ts` — Express routes. Add endpoints here.
- `api/src/seed.ts` — schema + seed data.
- `web/src/App.tsx` — the React list/detail view.
- `eval/` — the token eval runner and tasks.

## Conventions
- API routes are prefixed `/api`.
- Keep changes minimal and focused; small diffs.
- TypeScript strict mode is on.

## Don't read / don't touch (saves tokens)
- Do not read `node_modules/`, build output, or lockfiles.
- Do not read `results/*.json` — generated eval output.
- Default model is Sonnet. Do not switch to Opus.
